cv:me a schema:Person ;
    schema:name "Rishi Rajani" ;
    gr:kind "Person" ;
    schema:description "Data and knowledge engineer with approximately three years of experience in fintech and enterprise data, connecting business meaning with reliable data systems. Experienced in defining and documenting shared business metrics, standardizing data models, reconciling heterogeneous sources, and establishing data-quality practices and reporting adopted across business functions. Currently completing an M.Sc. in Computer Science at Universität Stuttgart, specializing in ontology engineering, knowledge graphs, description logics, and machine learning." ;
    schema:disambiguatingDescription "Data and knowledge engineer working on semantics, ontologies, data governance and quality" ;
    schema:email "rishirajani078@gmail.com" ;
    gr:location "Stuttgart, Germany (open to relocation)" ;
    gr:workedAs cv:r-nobel, cv:r-flexmoney, cv:r-flexmoney-am, cv:r-vmlyr, cv:r-ubisoft, cv:r-hog, cv:r-oracle ;
    gr:received cv:a-ironman ;
    gr:studied cv:e-msc, cv:e-be, cv:e-rubika ;
    gr:holds cv:c-udemy-python, cv:c-hackerrank-python ;
    gr:built cv:p-thesis, cv:p-loom, cv:p-heat, cv:p-arch, cv:p-rossmann ;
    gr:focusOn cv:g-gov, cv:g-kr, cv:g-de, cv:g-an, cv:g-sw, cv:g-games, cv:g-collab ;
    gr:speaks cv:l-en, cv:l-de, cv:l-hi, cv:l-mr, cv:l-sd .

cv:o-nobel a schema:Organization ;
    schema:name "Nobel Hygiene Pvt. Ltd." ;
    gr:kind "Organization" ;
    schema:description "Manufacturer of adult and baby hygiene products such as diapers and sanitary pads." .

cv:r-nobel a schema:OrganizationRole ;
    schema:name "Data Engineering Consultant" ;
    gr:kind "Role" ;
    schema:startDate "2023-10" ;
    schema:endDate "2024-03" ;
    gr:location "Mumbai, India" ;
    gr:highlight "Built a data integration and reporting proof of concept around existing SAP HANA and API services, implementing Python extraction, logging and transformation workflows, PostgreSQL storage, and Docker-hosted Apache Superset dashboards for sales leaders, the CFO and CMO.", "Standardized source-to-target field mappings and definitions, corrected duplicate API records, and reconciled delayed secondary-sales figures with manual sales-team reporting alongside primary- and secondary-sales stakeholders.", "Automated recurring data extraction and reporting, reducing manual reporting time by approximately 40%; coordinated access to on-premises virtual machines, APIs and data infrastructure.", "Developed an Amazon marketplace price tracker comparing company and competitor product listings to support commercial analysis: integrated the Amazon Selling Partner API to record competitor prices daily and the company's own product offers every four hours (buy-box eligibility, fulfilment-channel offer counts, landed prices, seller shipping times), batching requests within API rate limits.", "Automated daily ingestion of secondary-sales orders from the sales-force-automation platform's API into the analytics database, with retries, timeouts, saved fetch state for incremental loads, and a request/response log table for auditability.", "Packaged these scheduled Python jobs with Poetry and deployed them in a Docker container with cron, writing to Microsoft SQL Server through SQLAlchemy ORM models.", "Deployed the company's business-intelligence platform, NHPL BizIntel, on Apache Superset 3.0 with Docker Compose: company branding, a PostgreSQL metadata store with Redis, and database drivers for SAP HANA, SQL Server, MySQL and PostgreSQL.", "Built a custom Superset image with Firefox and GeckoDriver so scheduled email reports and alerts could render dashboard screenshots, delivered via Office 365 SMTP; added Prophet for forecasting and enabled native filters, Jinja templating and full CSV export." ;
    gr:at cv:o-nobel ;
    gr:used cv:s-python, cv:s-sap, cv:s-postgres, cv:s-docker, cv:s-superset, cv:s-etl, cv:s-integration, cv:s-s2t, cv:s-metricstd, cv:s-reconcile, cv:s-dq, cv:s-stakeholders, cv:s-rest, cv:s-mssql, cv:s-sqlalchemy, cv:s-pandas, cv:s-cron, cv:s-alerting .

cv:o-flexmoney a schema:Organization ;
    schema:name "Flexmoney Technologies Pvt. Ltd." ;
    gr:kind "Organization" ;
    schema:description "Consumer lending / fintech." .

cv:r-flexmoney a schema:OrganizationRole ;
    schema:name "Executive – Marketing Analytics (data & analytics engineering)" ;
    gr:kind "Role" ;
    schema:startDate "2021-03" ;
    schema:endDate "2023-03" ;
    gr:location "Mumbai, India" ;
    gr:highlight "Co-defined and documented transaction metrics with merchant-, lender- and product-facing stakeholders, reconciling competing interpretations of customer activity and implementing distinct business perspectives through SQL reporting.", "Owned launch-critical analytics for a new lending approval journey, defining multi-stage conversion funnels, writing SQL models and delivering dashboards required for product go-live.", "Converted manual Excel-based reporting into scalable Apache Superset dashboards and reusable queries; delivered analytics for six clients across two projects and ran demonstrations to support daily adoption by business and marketing teams.", "Built Python ELT pipelines connecting Google and Meta advertising data with website engagement and transaction activity via UTM parameters and session identifiers; analyzed high-volume merchant/product click funnels using CleverTap.", "Investigated suspicious transaction patterns associated with inactive merchant storefronts; screened merchant URLs programmatically, coordinated removal of confirmed defunct merchants, and identified duplicates and invalid URLs for master-data cleanup.", "Partnered with product and lending stakeholders on funnel improvements contributing to a reported 14–16% reduction in drop-offs; developed operational monitoring and anomaly alerts and briefed senior stakeholders regularly.", "Built 20+ dashboards and 20+ automated alert and reporting jobs, including a tracking system for lender API conversions shared in weekly lender calls, hourly business-performance monitoring for the festive season and daily automated MIS for top lenders; merchant, lender and engineering teams relied on them, including for network hygiene.", "Built a real-time tracker for lender transaction-API downtime; ahead of the 2022 festive sale, tightened alert definitions and shortened check intervals, and worked with Engineering to route Superset alerts into OpsGenie for on-call engineers.", "Created a Lender Report Card comparing lender performance across the network on key metrics, used by the business team in lender conversations.", "Optimized data-heavy Superset dashboards to a load success rate above 90% and removed inaccuracies; built trackers for No-Cost EMI offer spend, SMS campaign spend and digital-marketing performance, plus dashboards and MIS reports for new-to-bank lenders.", "Made the case, with supporting proof points, for a lending partner to restructure a policy that was rejecting repeat transactions; the change raised repeat rates by 100–150 basis points.", "Showed how lowering a lender's minimum transaction amount could grow its share on other merchants and reduce its dependence on its largest marketplace partner, and identified top-performing merchants to target.", "Pushed a lender to launch Cardless EMI beyond its largest marketplace partner, cutting one category of rejects from 20% to 5% and lifting success rates by about 10% on average; later encouraged it to restart the programme on other merchants, raising its success rate there by about 5%.", "Supplied data that led a lender to loosen its velocity-reject policy, and compared marketplace performance at a lender after a new marketplace launch to help scale it across the network.", "Studied users frequently rejected by top-performing lenders and identified segments for whom lender discovery could be disabled, improving API success rates.", "Helped create a standard operating process for tracking campaigns across the network, compared Facebook, CleverTap and database data as tracking sources, and tracked festive-season campaigns with CleverTap dashboards.", "Generated proof points from the December 2021 digital campaigns that helped improve the growth-hacking campaigns, contributing to over 2.5x growth in campaign activations; set up automated CleverTap journeys for users activating through lender campaigns, converting at about 4% for one lender.", "Built customer segments in CleverTap and the database for re-engagement, sale-event and new-to-bank drop-off campaigns, kept CleverTap user-profile data current so segments stayed accurate, and uncovered a backend bug that caused campaigns to reach unintended customers.", "Identified gaps in the data and flagged personal information exposed in datasets where it should not have been available.", "Analyzed surveys of transacting and ineligible customers to validate the new-to-bank business case and build user personas.", "Onboarded new colleagues on the database schema, Athena, Redshift, CleverTap and Superset.", "Led a team at the Flexathon 1.0 hackathon pitching Transactions as a Service, letting customers order with Cardless EMI directly from product-page widgets; the team received recognition." ;
    gr:at cv:o-flexmoney ;
    gr:used cv:s-kpi, cv:s-metricstd, cv:s-docs, cv:s-sql, cv:s-python, cv:s-etl, cv:s-superset, cv:s-clevertap, cv:s-funnel, cv:s-attribution, cv:s-kpifw, cv:s-mdm, cv:s-reconcile, cv:s-dq, cv:s-stakeholders, cv:s-requirements, cv:s-enablement, cv:s-athena, cv:s-redshift, cv:s-alerting, cv:s-segment, cv:s-survey, cv:s-privacy .

